      "decidedBy": "TASK-260715-ypo7yo r4, on TASK-260728-7ii1xz"
    },
    "keychain-access-groups": {
      "status": "prohibited",
      "portalCapability": false,
      "rationale": "The probe handles no credentials (TASK-260715-1r0fxv scope excludes SSH).",
      "reopensOnly": "This row reopens if, and only if, TASK-260715-1r0fxv gains a deliverable that stores a credential the probe must read back, AND a second macOS probe target must read the same item. Neither holds: the macOS probe exercises the NETunnelProviderManager lifecycle and a versioned app message, it stores no credential, and rule K1 excludes its root-context provider from Data Protection Keychain membership in any case. It does NOT reopen so that the probe can rehearse the production keychain shape - production carries no macOS keychain group either after rule K2, so there is no shape to rehearse.",
      "decidedBy": "TASK-260715-ypo7yo r5, on reviewer verdict 04 F1 (rule K2, applied to every withheld row rather than only the one the finding named)"
